cff-version: 1.2.0
title: Orbital Economics Observatory
message: >-
  If you use this software or the data it produces, please cite it
  using the metadata below.
type: software
authors:
  - given-names: Alex
    family-names: Dion
    orcid: "https://orcid.org/0000-0000-0000-0000"
repository-code: "https://github.com/alexdion-bot/orbital-economics-observatory"
url: "https://alexdion-bot.github.io/orbital-economics-observatory/"
abstract: >-
  An open estimate of the external cost imposed by every active satellite
  in low Earth orbit. Collision risk is computed shell by shell from the
  public GCAT catalogue using a kinetic model parameterised on MOCAT 4S,
  converted into monetary terms with the OPUS cost function, and
  decomposed into a congestion channel and a pollution channel following
  Rao, Burgess and Kaffine (2020) and Rao and Rondina (2025).
keywords:
  - space debris
  - orbital use fee
  - Pigouvian taxation
  - low Earth orbit
  - environmental economics
  - common pool resources
license: MIT
version: 1.0.0
date-released: "2026-08-08"
